# `answer.weigh(by)` where the answer may be `true` by Link is a call that nobody can follow: Boolean.prototype takes new names: the call is left to unseen code and `by` with it. Behind
# `if (v === true || v === false) return` no boolean goes on: the uses of v read a join that lets through every object and every primitive but the two. Where one way to a join carries no such
# comparison, nothing is excluded.
# f2 = keep, f3 = keepOnOneWay
